(*!
<summary>
Beckhoff EL2521: 1-channel pulse train output terminal (pulse/direction, up to 500 kHz).
</summary>
<description>
Requires enhanced operating mode (firmware 03 / hardware 02 or later supporting this preset)
and Predefined PDO Assignment Standard 32-bit (MDP 253/511).
Ch1 covers TxPDOs 0x1A01/0x1A05 and RxPDOs 0x1601/0x1607/0x1605.
Frequency remains a raw 16-bit command; target, counter feedback and counter preset are 32-bit.
Legacy and Standard 16-bit images are unsupported. Link each field separately and evaluate input validity.
Use one owner task; externally synchronize other access. Copies are data, not new links or atomic snapshots.
When used for I/O, link located fields or their containing buffers to the matching selected PDOs.
The record is not a packed wire buffer; compiler padding is not part of the device specification.
Unlinked/default values do not prove valid I/O. The caller evaluates bus/channel validity before use.
Use one owner task per instance and externally synchronize other access; multi-field snapshots are not atomic.
Copies store data without creating hardware links. Keep borrowed field references valid while consumers are bound.
This passive record performs no validation, synchronization, configuration or protocol advancement.
</description>
*)
TYPE EL2521 :
STRUCT
	Ch1 : PULSE_TRAIN_CHANNEL;
END_STRUCT
END_TYPE]]></Declaration>
  </DUT>
</TcPlcObject>
